xnu 0492: ring the bhi doorbell with an odd session

Measured 2026-11-27: the PBL reads the image and stops in `pbl_auth.c` with
`0xef0a0111` on an even `0x2a5a5a5a` session. The working SM8475 QCA6490
driver writes `(time & 0x3fffffff) | 1`, the 7a writes `1` and the donor
increments the inherited value, so every proven load uses an odd session.
Change only the session and keep the rest of the load byte for byte.

diff --git a/bsd/dev/mondrian_wifi.c b/bsd/dev/mondrian_wifi.c
--- a/bsd/dev/mondrian_wifi.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/mondrian_wifi.c
@@ -2116,8 +2116,13 @@
         wifi_log("W11 fsr clear rc=%d", fsr_rc);
         mondrian_log_flush_now();
     }
-    /* BHI_IMGTXDB is a 30-bit sequence, not a boolean. */
-    rc |= mondrian_mmio_try_wr32(wifi_bar + bhioff + 0x18, 0x2a5a5a5au);
+    /*
+     * BHI_IMGTXDB is a 30-bit session, not a boolean. The working
+     * SM8475 QCA6490 driver writes (time & 0x3fffffff) | 1 and the 7a
+     * writes 1, so the session is odd; 0x2a5a5a5a was the one value no
+     * working load used.
+     */
+    rc |= mondrian_mmio_try_wr32(wifi_bar + bhioff + 0x18, 0x2a5a5a5bu);
     WIFI_STAGE(17);
     wifi_log("W6 BHI trigger iova=0x%llx sbl=0x%x image=0x%x intvec=0x%x rc=0x%x",
         iova, image_size, got, intvec, rc);
